    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0ORNOT2C3",
        "Description": "NOT reading (input A, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.375) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-OR copy 3 of stage 0: Y = NOT(S1 AND C0), feeding T0OROUTC3.B. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_a5420bc23e4f40dabe31635470b596f1",
        "IdGuid": "43aaa3be-e8f7-451b-b261-62041839b5e7",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "8c8ee24c-f74b-4a66-84c2-aa261837eeba",
          "d76a8efc-2cb2-490d-b27a-3ce06c5eb203",
