    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1H1SUM10",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: sum stage of stage 1's partial sum (chain 10 of 10), Y = A1 XOR B1; this extra chain feeds the duplicated carry stage T1H2N5C7.B \u2014 one waveguide per pin. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_f2a2812491004427ae5e08467ee60a92",
        "IdGuid": "87b95474-a376-40b9-bbd2-14ec6a2f647a",
