    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1H2N5C3",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-OR copy 3 of stage 1: Y = NAND(C1, S1), feeding T1H2CARRYC3.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_e566ababe9ac4979b7686cd34e8d64ef",
        "IdGuid": "f23b2c1f-2afa-4180-aef7-ca13f053505c",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "37785445-d48d-4842-b9d9-6cc55587b9ce",
          "2eedba80-967a-4893-8a5a-3c1d574d9a3f",
