    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T2H1SUM7",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: sum stage of stage 2's partial sum (chain 7 of 7), Y = A2 XOR B2; this extra chain feeds the duplicated carry stage T2H2N5C4.B \u2014 one waveguide per pin. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_4174fb8cdf534ca3bc0bfab3433e54ac",
        "IdGuid": "e8286f3a-d5d7-4b81-bad0-cb341dbe4090",
